  "card_notes": [
   "Compared with the masks of record, the released model's mask extends one voxel further on about a quarter to a half of the lines at anterior-facing surfaces (anterior face 26\u201342 % vs posterior 6\u201314 % of lines, in-sample on MF278, MR243, MR257, MR263), where brain tissue just below the cut surface shows through the ice; the masks of record, and the earlier network (Dataset506) on brains outside its training set (anterior 8 % vs posterior 4\u20136 % of lines on MR257 and MR263), follow the cut face.",
   "In MR243 the mask the models were trained on is about one voxel short over the left hemisphere (left face 50 % vs right 16 % of lines): the voxel it leaves out is tissue-colored on the photograph, and the shortfall is inherited from the automatic mask the record was edited from (the two agree on 89 % of left-face lines, Dice 0.997). It was corrected after training (left face 13 % vs right 16 % of lines against the corrected label); on the anterior face the corrected left half now reaches further than the right (the model lies outside it on 18 % vs 33 % of lines, before 52 % vs 33 %).",
   "MF278's mask of record sits about half a voxel (0.2 mm) right of its blockface volume; every network, the earlier one included, places its mask about 0.2 mm left of it (x centroid -0.165 mm for the released model, -0.198 mm for Dataset506)."
  ],
